+# Reading List finishing pass
+
+Baseline: `009843a98bc64de22c50e0480e1187ee643726a9`.
+
+## Use
+
+Run **reading list** or **save to reading list** from the command palette, or
+use the new entries in a web page's context menu. The Reading List is a native
+full-window surface over the existing workspace. Escape returns to the list,
+then to the workspace. No new default keyboard binding is taken.
+
+A successful save first commits the page's address and browser container. Only
+then does capture start. "Link saved; no offline copy" is different from a
+saved article, and missing images are labeled. Saving again does not remove or
+refresh the item. Refresh is explicit and requires the original to be open in
+its saved container. Nothing is fetched automatically in the background.
+
+The native saved reader has search, mouse selection, UTF-8-safe keyboard
+selection, copy, code/table copy, horizontal scrolling for long preformatted
+blocks, text size controls, original-link navigation and saved paragraph
+anchors. Read state and archive state are independent. Opening an article does
+not mark it finished. The default To read filter places in-progress entries
+first. Search is over saved titles, URLs and container names, not full text.
+
+Snapshots reuse the existing Newsreader renderer; opening one creates no
+browser. A saved image is a PNG re-encoded from a loaded origin-clean image in
+the source page. Cross-origin tainted, unloaded, oversized or unsupported
+images retain alternative text with an incomplete-image indication. Capture
+neither fetches extra images nor bypasses browser origin restrictions.
+
+## Persistence and boundaries
+
+The lazy, process-shared worker serializes operations under `profile/reading`.
+The existing single-instance mechanism is still responsible for process-level
+profile ownership; this is not a new cross-process database lock.
+
+Each record is in `entries/<random-id>.json`. Immutable objects are in
+`objects/<sha256>.json`. Temp files are synchronized before replacement;
+Unix directory metadata is synchronized after replacement. An object is
+published before its entry reference. A failed refresh keeps the last valid
+snapshot. Hashes are checked before opening a saved copy. Changed external
+records are not silently overwritten. Unknown, malformed or oversized records
+are preserved with a warning instead of becoming an empty library.
+
+Capture tickets bind an entry generation to a stable browser instance,
+container, URL and navigation epoch. Deletion invalidates late captures. The
+capture transport has its own bounded allowance; normal inspector replies
+retain their existing 1 MiB limit. Reading payloads are not logged as previews.
+
+Only HTTP(S) addresses without embedded credentials are accepted. Query strings,
+fragments and container identity remain significant. The native snapshot format
+contains validated text blocks, explicit links and bounded PNGs, not executable
+HTML. No page-provided path is used as a filesystem path.
+
+Removed records are tombstoned; Undo is offered in the same session. **Remove
+is not secure erase.** Recovery records and superseded immutable objects are
+retained. There is no garbage collector or storage-quota management UI yet.
+Local filesystem permissions, not encryption, protect this saved content.
+The existing sync allowlist excludes the new reading directory. Incognito
+cannot initialize or save a Reading List. No accounts, telemetry, summaries,
+assistants, cloud services or new production dependencies are introduced.
+
+## Deliberate limits versus the broader design
+
+This is a first implementation, not a claim that the entire design is finished:
+
+* The Reading List is a native full-window surface, not a persistent Pane/tab.
+  Its entries and reading progress survive relaunch; the open surface does not
+  participate in session-pane restoration, pins, or saved layouts.
+* The existing extractor was strengthened, not replaced with Mozilla Readability.
+  It is a bounded read-only DOM traversal. It does not provide Readability's
+  extraction quality or an immutable cloned-document extraction pipeline.
+* Links are actionable references after the article rather than preserved inline
+  rich text. Emphasis is flattened. Tables preserve cells in horizontally
+  scrollable preformatted text; merged-cell fallback is explicitly disclosed.
+* Images are captured only when already decoded and origin-clean. This is not
+  full-web-page archival. Interactive embeds and mathematics have visible
+  fallbacks. Source addresses are retained for explicit original-page access.
+* The live reader receives the shared extraction/layout improvements, but the
+  new selection/find/clipboard controls are integrated into saved reading.
+  Full live-reader interaction parity remains separate work.
+* Multilingual text retention is tested; complex-script rendering, full Unicode
+  line breaking, screen-reader text-range selection and platform-specific IME
+  interaction have not been certified.
+* Reading font size is a per-window surface preference, not a persisted setting.
+* Welcome and sky/star artwork were not redesigned. The only related production
+  change suppresses hidden Home art animation under the Reading List. Welcome
+  labels, art seeds, and the broader visual/power acceptance pass remain open.
+
+## Checks
+
+Independent storage/model checks compile the actual production module without
+CEF or wgpu:
+
+```sh
+cargo test --manifest-path scripts/reading-check/Cargo.toml
+```
+
+This small test workspace resolves its own lockfile on first run. Review and
+retain that lockfile for repeatable CI; the production lockfile is unchanged.
+
+Actual extraction/capture sources in browser fixtures:
+
+```sh
+python3 scripts/reading-check/test_capture.py --chromium /path/to/chromium
+```
+
+Requires Python `playwright` and `Pillow`. It serves local fixtures only. On a
+managed host that prohibits loopback navigation, `--offline-dom` tests the
+real DOM/canvas code with inline images and explicitly skips the independent
+HTTP-origin test; it does not disable origin protections.
+
+Native build and integration checks (must run on the target platform):
+
+```sh
+cargo test --manifest-path spikes/composite/Cargo.toml --locked
+# Build the native macOS bundle through the existing project build procedure.
+python3 scripts/check-reading.py dist/nus.app
+python3 scripts/check-startup.py dist/nus.app
+```
+
+The native script uses temporary profiles, real capture/renderer actions, a
+loopback fixture page, saved images and exact code, then closes the source
+browser and relaunches with the fixture server stopped. It exercises semantic
+resume, find, archive/unarchive, confirmed removal/undo, basic accessibility
+structure and control containment. It records screenshots for human review.
+Fixed driver waits are generous but are not performance benchmarks. A timeout
+is a failure, not proof that the feature works on slower hardware.
+
+Before release, build and test macOS, Windows and Linux; run VoiceOver/NVDA,
+keyboard-only and manual pointer selection checks; review narrow/wide and
+light/dark screenshots; measure large-list/frame and shutdown behavior. Native
+build, Rust unit tests, GPU rendering, native end-to-end, visual acceptance,
+performance and platform accessibility were **not executed** in the patch's
+creation environment. See the accompanying validation report for executed
+checks and patch-application verification limits.
